<title>USA: St. Jude agrees with Q3 EPS estimates.</title>
<headline>St. Jude agrees with Q3 EPS estimates.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>St. Jude Medical Inc Chief Financial Officer Stephen Wilson said Tuesday the company was comfortable with analysts' estimates for third quarter earnings in a range of $0.44-$0.45 a share.</p>
<p>&quot;About $0.44 to $0.45 is where we should end up,&quot; Wilson said in a brief interview following a presentation to investors at a Dain Bosworth conference here.</p>
<p>The medical device maker earned $0.42 a share in the third quarter of 1995.</p>
<p>The stock was up 1/2 at 37-3/4 on Nasdaq.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
